## Summary: how you'll know testing passed or failed

| Signal | Pass | Fail |
|---|---|---|
| HTTP status | 200 everywhere | 422/502/503 anywhere |
| Known ticket retrieval | `INC-200003` found for its paraphrase | Not found, or ranked low |
| Self-match | Ticket never matches its own ID | It matches itself |
| Garbage input | `no_confident_match: true`, weak/no matches | Confident match to unrelated ticket |
| Severity override | P2 → `"High"`, `severity_source: "priority"` | Any other severity, or `source: "model"` |
| Open ticket resolution_type | `"not recorded"` | An actual resolution type invented |
| Grounding | `grounded_ticket_ids` ⊆ `agent3_result` match IDs | An ID appears that wasn't in agent3 |
| Orchestrator consistency | `agent2`/`agent3`/`agent4` agree on the same ticket | Contradictory modules/IDs, or `null` sub-results |

